==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|seewey}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sǣweġ||a seaway, a path through the sea}}, equivalent to {{com|en|sea|way}}. Compare {{cog|stq|Seegong|t=seaway, swell}}, {{cog|de|Seegang|t=seaway, swell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|iːweɪ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[lane]] or [[route]] at [[sea]] that is [[regularly]] used by [[ship]]s; a [[sea lane]] or [[trade route]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} An [[inland]] [[waterway]] used by [[seagoing]] [[shipping]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[headway]] of a [[vessel]].

